---

A style of semantics that defines the meaning of programs by syntactically transforming terms according to reduction rules, specifying execution either step-by-step (${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/small-step-structural-operational-semantics-sos.td")}) or as a direct relation to final values (${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/big-step-natural-operational-semantics.td")}).
